% ----------------------------------------------------------- parameters ------
\section*{Primary parameters}
\textbf{Mission profile (GUI inputs):}\ payload mass, payload bounding box, target endurance, take-off run, motor / battery class, climb performance.\\
\textbf{Fuselage geometry (computed):}\ \texttt{Fuselage\_Length}, \texttt{Fuselage\_Width}, \texttt{Fuselage\_Height}, \\\texttt{Number\_of\_Bulkheads}, \texttt{Number\_of\_Frames}, \texttt{Stringer\_Count}, \texttt{Longeron\_Count}, \texttt{Lightening\_Hole\_Pattern}.\\
\textbf{Internal payload (placed by the GUI):}\ battery (mass, X-station), motor (mass, X-station = 0), ESC (X-station), flight controller (X-station), receiver / GPS, optional cargo bay.\\
\textbf{Landing gear (CG-based):}\ \texttt{Gear\_Station\_X} (computed from the CG solver), \texttt{Gear\_Type} (tail-dragger / tricycle), \texttt{Wheel\_Diameter}, \texttt{Wheel\_Width}, \texttt{Wheels\_per\_Strut}.\\
\textbf{Configuration metadata (SQLite, Grade 5):}\ \texttt{Config\_Name}, \texttt{Date\_Created}, \texttt{Mission\_Profile}, \texttt{Notes}.

% ----------------------------------------------------------- aim -------------
\section*{Aim / technical goals (Grade 5)}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Apply SAE AeroDesign Brasil 2026 design constraints (shipping-box dimensions, max take-off mass) inside the GUI as hard limits on the parameters.
    \item Standardise structural member sizes (balsa thicknesses, plywood thicknesses, spruce stringer cross-sections) so the output can go straight to manufacturing.
    \item Automatic instantiation of bulkheads, frames, stringers, longerons and lightening cut-outs through PowerCopies.
    \item Instantiation-upon-instantiation for the wheel on the strut, with the strut placed at the CG-driven station.
    \item GitLab LiU activity (commits / branches / merge requests) as Grade-5 proof of individual activity, at least two commits per member per week.
    \item SQLite save / load of mission profiles + standard configurations from the GUI.
\end{itemize}

